* Tu cafe ka Wi-Fi use karega apni side se. Mac mini ghar ka Wi-Fi/broadband use karega apni side se. Dono online honge tabhi Tailscale connect karega.\n\n**Agar ghar pe internet nahi hai → Mac mini online nahi → tu remote access nahi kar payega. Simple.**\n\n### Kya chahiye ghar pe:\n\n| Cheez | Chahiye? | Kitna kharcha |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| **Broadband connection** | ✅ Haan, mandatory | ₹500-800/month (Jio Fiber, Airtel, BSNL — basic plan kafi hai) |\n| **Wi-Fi router** | ✅ Haan (mostly broadband ke saath free milta hai) | ₹0 (included) ya ₹1,000-2,000 alag se |\n| **Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se connect karna** | ✅ Haan — Mac mini mein Wi-Fi 7 built-in hai | ₹0 |\n| **Ethernet cable (optional)** | Better than Wi-Fi for always-on server | ₹200-500 (stable connection, recommended) |\n\n### Agar ghar pe already broadband hai:\n\nToh bas Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se connect kar, Tailscale install kar, Ollama setup kar — done. Koi extra kharcha nahi.\n\n### Agar ghar pe broadband NAHI hai:\n\nToh ₹500-800/month ka basic plan lagwa. Jio Fiber ka ₹399 wala plan bhi chalega — tujhe video streaming nahi karni Mac mini se, sirf text data (prompts + responses) jaayega jo 1-2 KB/sec hai. Sabse sasta internet plan bhi kaafi hai.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro tip:** Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se nahi, **Ethernet cable** se router se connect kar. Wi-Fi se bhi chalega, lekin Ethernet zyada stable hai — 24/7 server ke liye disconnect nahi hoga kabhi. Ek ₹200 ka LAN cable laga de, tension-free.","thinking":"The user is asking two simple, practical questions:\n\n1. If they have an inverter at home, do they need a UPS for the Mac mini? Will the inverter handle the power backup?\n2. Does the Mac mini need to be connected to the internet (Wi-Fi) at home for the user to access it remotely from a cafe/library? Do they need to get a Wi-Fi connection at home?\n\nThese are straightforward questions. Let me answer directly without over-researching.\n\n1. **Inverter vs UPS**: An inverter at home will work fine for keeping the Mac mini running during power cuts. The Mac mini uses very little power (10-15W idle, 40-60W under load). \n\nA regular inverter should handle this fine, though there's a brief switchover gap when mains cuts out that a true UPS avoids entirely with instant switching. Still, most modern inverters switch fast enough that the Mac mini won't even blink. For the second question, yes - the Mac mini absolutely needs to stay connected to the internet at home for remote access via Tailscale to work while they're out at a cafe.\n\nThese are straightforward questions, so I'll just answer directly without needing an artifact.\n\n"}
{"step_index":121,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:59:01Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n@[Quote] Mere ko yeh nahi samajh mein aaya. Yeh tune kyun bola? Ek-do line mein bata de. Agar research karna hai, to achhe se research karke hi bata sakta hai. Abhi mere ko ek aur doubt aaya ki agar Mac mini ghar pe kaise khula rahega, bina koi desktop ke, bina kuch rahe? Kyunki main apna MacBook Air to kahin aur lekar ghoom raha hoon, to usko kaise karunga main? Access bas Mac mini start rakhna padega hamesha, wo to samajh gaya, par bina kisi screen ke, bina kisi cheez ke kaise hoga? Ye koi problem hai didi ya nahi? @[Quote] aur ye jo Ethernet ka upar maine code kiya hai, ye bhi tune same wahi bola hai na, protip mein shayad short mein bata na. \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-01T18:29:01+05:30.\n\nThe user has mentioned some items in the form @[ITEM]. Here is extra information about the items that were mentioned by the user, in the order that they appear:\n\n@[Quote] is a [Text Block]:\nEthernet cable (optional)\nBetter than Wi-Fi for always-on server\n₹200-500 (stable connection, recommended)\n@[Quote] is a [Text Block]:\nPro tip: Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se nahi, Ethernet cable se router se connect kar. Wi-Fi se bhi chalega, lekin Ethernet zyada stable hai — 24/7 server ke liye disconnect nahi hoga kabhi. Ek ₹200 ka LAN cable laga de, tension-free.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:59:03Z","content":"## Ethernet Cable Kyun? (2 Lines)\n\nWi-Fi sometimes raat ko 2 baje disconnect ho jaata hai — router restart hua, signal weak hua. Agar Mac mini Wi-Fi pe hai aur disconnect hua, toh tu cafe se access nahi kar payega. **Ethernet cable = physical wire jo router se Mac mini mein lagta hai. Ye kabhi disconnect nahi hota.** Bas itna. Haan, table aur pro tip dono same baat hai.\n\n---\n\n## Mac mini bina screen ke kaise chalega?\n\n**Koi problem nahi hai. Mac mini bina monitor, bina keyboard, bina mouse ke chal sakta hai.** Isko \"headless\" bolte hain — bahut common hai, log server ke liye exactly aise hi use karte hain.\n\nSetup ek baar karna padega (pehli baar monitor lagake):\n\n| Step | Kya karna hai | Ek baar ya hamesha |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| **1** | Mac mini pehli baar monitor + keyboard lagake setup kar — Apple ID, Wi-Fi/Ethernet, Ollama install | Ek baar |\n| **2** | System Settings → Energy → **\"Prevent automatic sleeping\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **3** | System Settings → General → Sharing → **\"Remote Login\" (SSH)** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **4** | System Settings → General → Sharing → **\"Screen Sharing\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **5** | System Settings → Energy → **\"Start up automatically after power failure\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **6** | Monitor/keyboard nikal de. Mac mini chalta rahega bina screen ke | Done |\n\n**Ab kaise access karega bina screen ke:**\n\n| Kahan se | Kaise |\n|:---|:---|\n| **Ghar mein MacBook Air se** | Finder → Network → Mac mini dikhega → Screen Sharing se poora desktop dikha dega tere Air pe |\n| **Bahar se MacBook Air se** | Tailscale se connect kar → SSH ya Screen Sharing — same cheez, internet ke through |\n\nMac mini ko screen ki zaroorat nahi hai chalne ke liye. Wo background mein Ollama chala raha hai, internet se connected hai, aur tera prompt ka wait kar raha hai. Jaise tera Wi-Fi router bina screen ke 24/7 chalta hai — Mac mini bhi waise hi chalega.","thinking":"The user has three questions:\n\n1. Why did I recommend Ethernet cable? They want a 1-2 line explanation.\n2. How will Mac mini work without any screen/monitor/keyboard at home? They're taking their MacBook Air elsewhere, so how does Mac mini stay running without a display?\n3. Confirming that the Ethernet cable thing in the table and the pro tip are the same thing.\n\nLet me answer simply:\n\n1. Ethernet: Wi-Fi sometimes disconnects — 2 AM ko Wi-Fi drop hua, Mac mini offline ho gaya, tu cafe mein access nahi kar payega. Ethernet cable kabhi disconnect nahi hota. That's it.\n2. Headless Mac mini is actually totally normal — set it to never sleep, enable Remote Login (SSH), and it just boots automatically and accepts SSH/Screen Sharing connections from the MacBook Air without needing a monitor at all.\n3. Yes, same thing — Ethernet cable is just the LAN cable connecting Mac mini to the router.\n\nThese are straightforward, I'll answer directly.\n\n"}
